well above forecast.** A missing unit costs 10 (the 7 margin plus the 3 penalty). An extra unit costs at most 4, and usually less, because it is sold in the next 1–2 days. That puts the right level at about the 0.7 quantile of 2-day demand, roughly 1.17–1.2× forecast or higher. Candidate 7's 40 units against a mean of 34.5 fits that best.\n\n**4. Product 1 also benefits from candidate 7's larger orders.** A missing unit costs 9. An extra unit is usually carried into the next batch (it lasts 5 days), costing about 3–5 rather than its full price of 10. Moving from 50 units (candidate 1) to 55 (candidate 7) cuts the average shortfall from about 5.1 to about 2.8 units per batch. That is worth roughly 8–12 per batch, or about 100–140 over the 30 days.\n\n**5. Risks for candidate 7.** On the morning of day 10, about 155 of 160 places are filled on average. When demand is low, part of the 108-unit delivery of product 1 can overflow and be lost. I estimate this costs about 30–50 on average. The overflow only happens when there is already extra stock that would partly expire anyway. That is less than the gain from fewer shortages. Candidate 7 orders the most of the every-2-days plans, but it is still not excessive for either product."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 359, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5749, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 359}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T20:02:34.256Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPYtKNm5qRtPqvPfgSwp"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "cont